	Return value: TRUE => Success, FALSE => Failure, invlid parameter value. ]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>ptr</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Pointer to external string memory (buffer) ]]></Comment><Type GUID="{18071995-0000-0000-0000-000000000018}">PVOID</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>size</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Max. byte size of external string memory (buffer) ]]></Comment><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>Clear</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Resets the string (sets empty string value) ]]></Comment></Method><Method><Name>Concat</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ The length of sSource will be calculated and concat to the actual string.
If sSource string extends the available buffer space then bOverflow output will be set to TRUE.
In this case only subset of characters will be concatenated (up to the max. available buffer space).
If succeeded (one or all characters are concatenated) then the return value is TRUE.
The return value is FALSE if string object is not initialized (buffer Size and/or Ptr properties are not set).
