ING(17)</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>144</ReturnBitSize><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__getsSrvNetID</Name><ReturnType Namespace="Tc2_System">T_AmsNetID</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>192</ReturnBitSize><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__gettAdsTimeout</Name><ReturnType>TIME</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__getthrottleTimes</Name><ReturnType Namespace="Tc2_TcpIp">T_ThrottleTimes</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>416</ReturnBitSize><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>AbortReq</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ This method activates the abort command. Abort command has higher priority than close or open command.
In busy state:
	If allready aborting => AbortReq returns TRUE and busy state, completes abort, returns aborted state + (first/previous set) abort reason.
	If allready closing => AbortReq returns TRUE and busy state, completes close, executes and completes abort, returns aborted state + abort reason.
	If allready opening => AbortReq returns TRUE and busy state, completes open, if successfully opened then executes and completes close, executes and completes abort, returns aborted state + abort reason.
Not in busy state:
	If state closed (idle/aborted/failed/completed) => AbortReq returns TRUE and aborted state + abort reason.
	If state opened => AbortReq returns TRUE and busy state, executes and completes close, executes and completes abort, returns aborted state + abort reason.
]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>ipReason</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Interface pointer to abort reason information ]]></Comment><Type Namespace="Tc3_Collections">I_ServiceErrorClass</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>ipResult</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Interface pointer to service state and result information ]]></Comment><Type Namespace="Tc3_Collections">I_AsyncServiceResultClass</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter><Properties><Property><Name>conditionalshow</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>CloseReq</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ This method activates the close command.
In busy state:
	If allready aborting => CloseReq returns TRUE and busy state, completes abort, returns aborted state + abort reason.
	If allready closing => CloseReq returns TRUE and busy state, completes close, returns succeeded or failed (close) state.
	If allready opening => CloseReq returns TRUE and busy state, completes open, if opened then executes and completes close, returns succeeded or failed (close) state.
Not in busy state:
	If state closed (idle/aborted/failed/completed) => CloseReq returns TRUE and succeeded (close) state.
	If state opened => CloseReq returns TRUE and busy state, executes and completes close, returns succeeded or failed (close) state.
]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>ipResult</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Interface pointer to service state and result information ]]></Comment><Type Namespace="Tc3_Collections">I_AsyncServiceResultClass</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter><Properties><Property><Name>conditionalshow</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>HostEquals</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Compares local or remote host address string ]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>sAddr</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Host address string to be compared to ]]></Comment><Type Namespace="Tc2_System">T_IPv4Addr</Type><BitSize>128</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>bLocal</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ TRUE=> compare to local address host string, FALSE=> compare to remote addres host string ]]></Comment><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>PortEquals</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Compares local or remote port address number ]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>nPort</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Port number to be compared to ]]></Comment><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>bLocal</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ TRUE=> compare to local address port number, FALSE=> compare to remote addres port number ]]></Comment><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize></Parameter></Method></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Tc3_Sockets">I_SocketConnectionClass</Name><BitSize>64</BitSize><ExtendsType GUID="{18071995-0000-0000-0000-000000000018}">PVOID</ExtendsType><Method><Name>__geteLinkStatus</Name><ReturnType Namespace="Tc3_Sockets">E_TcpLinkStatus</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Properties><Property><Name>property</Name></Property></Properties></Method><Method><Name>__geteState</Name><ReturnType Namespace="Tc3_Collect